(* Row Echelon Form \(REF\): A matrix is in REF if: \(a\) All zero rows are at the bottom.) Tj
T*
(\(b\) The leading entry \(first non-zero number from the left, pivot\) of each non-zero) Tj
T*
(row is strictly to the right of the leading entry of the row above it. \(c\) All) Tj
T*
(entries below each pivot are zero.) Tj
T*
(* Reduced Row Echelon Form \(RREF\): An REF matrix where every pivot entry is equal to) Tj
T*
(1, and each pivot 1 is the ONLY non-zero entry in its entire column.) Tj
T*
(* Rank of Matrix \(rho\): Defined as the maximum number of linearly independent row or) Tj
T*
(column vectors. Computationally, rho\(A\) equals the total count of non-zero rows in) Tj
T*
(its row echelon form. For an m x n matrix, rho\(A\) <= min\(m, n\). A matrix of order n) Tj
T*
(with rho\(A\) = n is non-singular with det\(A\) != 0.) Tj
