(* The Rouche-Capelli Theorem \(Fundamental Existence & Uniqueness Theorem\):) Tj
T*
(1. Inconsistent System \(No Solution\): If rho\(A\) < rho\(A | B\). Geometrically,) Tj
T*
(planes/hyperplanes do not intersect at a common manifold.) Tj
T*
(2. Consistent System with Unique Solution: If rho\(A\) = rho\(A | B\) = n \(where n is the) Tj
T*
(number of unknown variables\). Det\(A\) != 0.) Tj
T*
(3. Consistent System with Infinitely Many Solutions: If rho\(A\) = rho\(A | B\) = r < n. The) Tj
T*
(system possesses \(n - r\) independent arbitrary parameters \(degrees of freedom\).) Tj
T*
(* Homogeneous Linear Systems \(AX = 0\): Always consistent since X = 0 \(the trivial) Tj
T*
(zero vector\) is always a solution. If rho\(A\) = n, only the trivial solution exists.) Tj
T*
(If rho\(A\) < n \(i.e., det\(A\) = 0\), non-trivial non-zero solutions exist, spanning the) Tj
